### Description
This Terraform configuration sets up an RDS database with blue/green deployment capabilities. It also creates an IAM instance profile named "ec2_eb_profile1" for use with Elastic Beanstalk environments. The database is named "my_db", and a snapshot of the database is taken before any deployment.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_iam_instance_profile" "ec2_eb_profile1" {
  name = "ec2_eb_profile1"

  roles = [
    aws_iam_role.ec2_eb_role.name
  ]
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "ec2_eb_role" {
  name = "ec2_eb_role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "ec2.amazonaws.com"
        }
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy" "ec2_eb_policy" {
  name = "ec2_eb_policy"
  role = aws_iam_role.ec2_eb_role.id

  policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = [
          "logs:*",
          "cloudwatch:*",
          "ec2:*",
          "elasticbeanstalk:*",
          "autoscaling:*",
          "s3:*",
          "sns:*",
          "rds:*"
        ]
        Effect = "Allow"
        Resource = "*"
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_db_instance" "rds_database" {
  instance_class = "db.t3.micro"
  db_name        = "my_db"
  username       = "admin"
  password       = "securepassword"
  engine         = "mysql"
  allocated_storage = 20

  custom_iam_instance_profile = aws_iam_instance_profile.ec2_eb_profile1.name

  blue_green_update {
    enabled = true
  }

  lifecycle {
    create_before_destroy = true
  }
}

resource "aws_db_snapshot" "rds_snapshot" {
  db_instance_identifier = aws_db_instance.rds_database.identifier
  db_snapshot_identifier = "my_db_snapshot"
}
```

### Explanation
1. **Provider Configuration**: Sets the AWS provider with a specific region (`us-west-2`).
2. **IAM Instance Profile**: Creates an IAM instance profile named "ec2_eb_profile1".
3. **IAM Role**: Defines an IAM role named "ec2_eb_role" with a trust policy allowing EC2 to assume the role.
4. **IAM Role Policy**: Attaches a policy to the IAM role granting various permissions needed for Elastic Beanstalk and related services.
5. **RDS Database**: Creates an RDS MySQL instance with blue/green deployment enabled. The instance class is set to `db.t3.micro`, and the database name is "my_db". The custom IAM instance profile is associated with the RDS instance.
6. **DB Snapshot**: Takes a snapshot of the RDS database before deployment, naming it "my_db_snapshot".

This configuration ensures that the RDS database is set up with blue/green deployment capabilities and that a snapshot is taken before any deployment, fulfilling the requirements specified in the prompt.

