### Description
This Terraform configuration sets up a non-alias AWS Route 53 record linked to a private Route 53 zone named "internal.example53.com". The private zone is associated with an AWS VPC named "main". The VPC is configured with DNS support and hostnames enabled.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_vpc" "main" {
  cidr_block           = "10.0.0.0/16"
  enable_dns_hostnames = true
  enable_dns_support   = true

  tags = {
    Name = "main"
  }
}

resource "aws_route53_zone" "private_zone" {
  name = "internal.example53.com"

  vpc {
    vpc_id = aws_vpc.main.id
  }

  tags = {
    Name = "private_zone"
  }
}

resource "aws_route53_record" "non_alias_record" {
  name    = "example.internal.example53.com"
  type    = "A"
  zone_id = aws_route53_zone.private_zone.zone_id
  ttl     = 300
  records = ["10.0.0.1"]

  tags = {
    Name = "non_alias_record"
  }
}
```

### Explanation
1. **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured to use the "us-west-2" region.
2. **VPC Resource**: An AWS VPC named "main" is created with a CIDR block of "10.0.0.0/16". DNS support and hostnames are enabled.
3. **Route 53 Zone Resource**: A private Route 53 zone named "internal.example53.com" is created and associated with the VPC "main".
4. **Route 53 Record Resource**: A non-alias Route 53 record named "example.internal.example53.com" is created within the private zone. The record type is "A", with a TTL of 300 seconds and a single record pointing to "10.0.0.1".

