### Description
This Terraform script creates an AWS EKS cluster named "example" and adds the "vpc-cni" addon to it. The script also defines an IAM role required for the EKS cluster.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "eks_cluster_role" {
  name = "eks-cluster-role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "eks.amazonaws.com"
        }
      },
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "eks_cluster_policy" {
  policy_arn = "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AmazonEKSClusterPolicy"
  role       = aws_iam_role.eks_cluster_role.name
}

resource "aws_eks_cluster" "example_cluster" {
  name     = "example"
  role_arn = aws_iam_role.eks_cluster_role.arn

  vpc_config {
    subnet_ids = ["subnet-0123456789abcdef0", "subnet-0fedcba9876543210"]
  }

  depends_on = [
    aws_iam_role_policy_attachment.eks_cluster_policy,
  ]
}

resource "aws_eks_addon" "example_addon" {
  cluster_name = aws_eks_cluster.example_cluster.name
  addon_name   = "vpc-cni"
}
```

### Explanation
1. **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured to use the "us-west-2" region.
2. **IAM Role**: An IAM role named "eks-cluster-role" is created with an assume role policy that allows EKS to assume the role.
3. **IAM Role Policy Attachment**: The "AmazonEKSClusterPolicy" policy is attached to the IAM role.
4. **EKS Cluster**: An EKS cluster named "example" is created with the specified IAM role and VPC configuration. The cluster depends on the IAM role policy attachment to ensure proper permissions.
5. **EKS Addon**: The "vpc-cni" addon is added to the EKS cluster.

This configuration ensures that the EKS cluster and its addon are correctly set up with the necessary IAM roles and permissions.

