### Description
This Terraform configuration creates an AWS S3 bucket with a specified name and sets its ownership controls to ensure that the bucket owner automatically owns and has full control over every object in the bucket. The configuration includes the creation of the S3 bucket and the subsequent configuration of its ownership controls, ensuring proper resource linking and dependency management.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # Specify the desired AWS region
}

# Define the S3 bucket resource
resource "aws_s3_bucket" "my_s3_bucket" {
  bucket = "my-unique-bucket-name"  # Specify a unique bucket name
  acl    = "private"                # Set the ACL to private
}

# Configure ownership controls for the S3 bucket
resource "aws_s3_bucket_ownership_controls" "my_s3_bucket_ownership_controls" {
  bucket = aws_s3_bucket.my_s3_bucket.id  # Reference the bucket ID

  rule {
    object_ownership = "BucketOwnerPreferred"  # Set object ownership to BucketOwnerPreferred
  }
}
```

### Explanation
1. **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured with a specific region (`us-west-2`). You can change this to any valid AWS region as needed.
2. **S3 Bucket Resource**: An S3 bucket named `my-unique-bucket-name` is created with private access control.
3. **Ownership Controls**: The ownership controls for the S3 bucket are configured to set the object ownership to `BucketOwnerPreferred`, ensuring that the bucket owner automatically owns and has full control over every object in the bucket. The `bucket` attribute in the `aws_s3_bucket_ownership_controls` resource references the ID of the previously created S3 bucket.

