### Description
This Terraform configuration creates an AWS SageMaker endpoint along with its necessary dependencies, including an S3 bucket for data capture and a SageMaker model. The configuration ensures that all required resources are properly linked and that the SageMaker endpoint is correctly set up with the specified configurations.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

# IAM Role for SageMaker Model
resource "aws_iam_role" "sagemaker_role" {
  name = "sagemaker-execution-role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "sagemaker.amazonaws.com"
        }
      }
    ]
  })
}

# SageMaker Model
resource "aws_sagemaker_model" "sagemaker_model" {
  name               = "my-sagemaker-model"
  execution_role_arn = aws_iam_role.sagemaker_role.arn

  primary_container {
    image = "123456789012.dkr.ecr.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/my-model:latest"
  }
}

# S3 Bucket for Data Capture
resource "aws_s3_bucket" "sagemaker_data_capture_bucket" {
  bucket = "my-sagemaker-data-capture-bucket-${random_string.suffix.result}"
  acl    = "private"

  tags = {
    Name = "SageMaker Data Capture Bucket"
  }
}

resource "random_string" "suffix" {
  length  = 8
  special = false
}

# SageMaker Endpoint Configuration
resource "aws_sagemaker_endpoint_configuration" "sagemaker_endpoint_configuration" {
  name = "my-sagemaker-endpoint-config"

  production_variants {
    variant_name           = "variant-1"
    model_name             = aws_sagemaker_model.sagemaker_model.name
    initial_instance_count = 1
    instance_type          = "ml.m5.large"
  }

  data_capture_config {
    destination_s3_uri         = "s3://${aws_s3_bucket.sagemaker_data_capture_bucket.bucket}/capture/"
    initial_sampling_percentage = 100
    enable_capture            = true
  }
}

# SageMaker Endpoint
resource "aws_sagemaker_endpoint" "sagemaker_endpoint" {
  name                 = "my-sagemaker-endpoint"
  endpoint_config_name = aws_sagemaker_endpoint_configuration.sagemaker_endpoint_configuration.name

  tags = {
    Name = "SageMaker Endpoint"
  }
}
```

### Explanation
1. **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured to use the `us-west-2` region.
2. **IAM Role**: An IAM role named `sagemaker-execution-role` is created, allowing SageMaker to assume this role.
3. **SageMaker Model**: A SageMaker model is defined with the specified execution role and a primary container pointing to a Docker image.
4. **S3 Bucket**: An S3 bucket is created for storing data capture logs. A random suffix is appended to the bucket name to ensure uniqueness.
5. **SageMaker Endpoint Configuration**: The endpoint configuration specifies a production variant using the previously created model and configures data capture to the S3 bucket.
6. **SageMaker Endpoint**: Finally, the SageMaker endpoint is created using the endpoint configuration.

This configuration ensures that all dependencies are correctly set up and that the SageMaker endpoint is ready for use.

