### Description
This Terraform configuration creates the latest Amazon Linux 2 AMI, defines a launch template with specific CPU options (2 cores and 2 threads per core), and then creates an EC2 instance using that launch template. The configuration ensures that all dependencies are correctly handled, and it adheres to the requirements specified in the prompt.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # Specify your desired AWS region
}

data "aws_ami" "latest_amazon_linux_2" {
  most_recent = true
  owners      = ["amazon"]

  filter {
    name   = "name"
    values = ["amzn2-ami-hvm-*-x86_64-gp2"]
  }
}

resource "aws_launch_template" "launch_template_example" {
  name          = "launch-template-example"
  image_id      = data.aws_ami.latest_amazon_linux_2.id
  instance_type = "t3.micro"

  cpu_options {
    core_count       = 2
    threads_per_core = 2
  }
}

resource "aws_instance" "instance_example" {
  launch_template {
    id      = aws_launch_template.launch_template_example.id
    version = "$Latest"
  }
}
```

### Explanation
1. **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured with the region `us-west-2`. You can change this to your preferred region.
2. **Data Source for AMI**: A data source `aws_ami` is used to fetch the latest Amazon Linux 2 AMI.
3. **Launch Template**: An `aws_launch_template` resource is created with the fetched AMI ID and specifies the instance type `t3.micro`. The CPU options are set to 2 cores and 2 threads per core.
4. **EC2 Instance**: An `aws_instance` resource is created using the launch template. The instance will use the latest version of the launch template.

This configuration ensures that the latest Amazon Linux 2 AMI is used, and the EC2 instance is launched with the specified CPU options.

