### Description
This Terraform program creates an AWS Virtual Private Cloud (VPC) with an example CIDR block and IPv6 enabled. It also creates a subnet within the VPC and an egress-only Internet Gateway associated with the VPC.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_vpc" "main_vpc" {
  cidr_block                = "10.0.0.0/16"
  assign_generated_ipv6_cidr_block = true
  enable_dns_support        = true
  enable_dns_hostnames      = true

  tags = {
    Name = "MainVPC"
  }
}

resource "aws_subnet" "main_subnet" {
  vpc_id            = aws_vpc.main_vpc.id
  cidr_block        = "10.0.1.0/24"
  availability_zone = "us-west-2a"

  tags = {
    Name = "MainSubnet"
  }
}

resource "aws_egress_only_internet_gateway" "main_egress_only_igw" {
  vpc_id = aws_vpc.main_vpc.id

  tags = {
    Name = "MainEgressOnlyIGW"
  }
}
```

### Explanation
1. **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured to use the `us-west-2` region.
2. **AWS VPC**: A VPC is created with the CIDR block `10.0.0.0/16` and IPv6 enabled (`assign_generated_ipv6_cidr_block = true`). DNS support and hostnames are enabled.
3. **AWS Subnet**: A subnet is created within the VPC with the CIDR block `10.0.1.0/24` and placed in the `us-west-2a` availability zone.
4. **AWS Egress-Only Internet Gateway**: An egress-only Internet Gateway is created and associated with the VPC.

This configuration ensures that the VPC, subnet, and egress-only Internet Gateway are properly set up and interconnected.

