### Description
This Terraform configuration creates two AWS Virtual Private Clouds (VPCs) and establishes a peering connection between them. The VPCs are configured with basic settings, and the peering connection is set to automatically accept.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

# Create the first VPC
resource "aws_vpc" "vpc1" {
  cidr_block           = "10.0.0.0/16"
  enable_dns_support   = true
  enable_dns_hostnames = true

  tags = {
    Name = "VPC1"
  }
}

# Create the second VPC
resource "aws_vpc" "vpc2" {
  cidr_block           = "10.1.0.0/16"
  enable_dns_support   = true
  enable_dns_hostnames = true

  tags = {
    Name = "VPC2"
  }
}

# Establish a peering connection between the two VPCs
resource "aws_vpc_peering_connection" "vpc_peering_connection" {
  vpc_id      = aws_vpc.vpc1.id
  peer_vpc_id = aws_vpc.vpc2.id
  auto_accept = true

  tags = {
    Name = "VPC1-to-VPC2-Peering"
  }
}
```

This configuration sets up two VPCs with the specified CIDR blocks and enables DNS support and hostnames. It then creates a VPC peering connection between them, with automatic acceptance enabled. All resources are tagged for easy identification.

