### Description
This Terraform program creates two AWS Chime Voice Connectors, both with encryption enabled, and groups them together into a single AWS Chime Voice Connector Group. The configuration ensures that the dependencies between the resources are correctly managed, with the voice connectors being created before they are added to the group.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-1"
}

resource "aws_chime_voice_connector" "voice_connector_1" {
  name               = "VoiceConnector1"
  require_encryption = true
  aws_region         = "us-east-1"
}

resource "aws_chime_voice_connector" "voice_connector_2" {
  name               = "VoiceConnector2"
  require_encryption = true
  aws_region         = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_chime_voice_connector_group" "voice_connector_group" {
  name = "VoiceConnectorGroup"

  connector {
    voice_connector_id = aws_chime_voice_connector.voice_connector_1.id
    priority           = 1
  }

  connector {
    voice_connector_id = aws_chime_voice_connector.voice_connector_2.id
    priority           = 2
  }
}
```

This Terraform configuration does the following:
1. Sets up the AWS provider with the region `us-east-1`.
2. Creates two AWS Chime Voice Connectors (`voice_connector_1` and `voice_connector_2`) with encryption enabled.
3. Groups these two voice connectors into a single AWS Chime Voice Connector Group (`voice_connector_group`), specifying their priorities.

