### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket" "my_s3_bucket" {
  bucket = "my-example-bucket-12345"
  acl    = "private"
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket_cors_configuration" "my_s3_bucket_cors_config" {
  bucket = aws_s3_bucket.my_s3_bucket.id

  cors_rule {
    allowed_headers = ["*"]
    allowed_methods = ["PUT", "POST"]
    allowed_origins = ["https://s3-website-test.hashicorp.com"]
    expose_headers  = ["ETag"]
    max_age_seconds = 3000
  }

  cors_rule {
    allowed_methods = ["GET"]
    allowed_origins = ["*"]
  }
}
```

This configuration does the following:
1. Sets up the AWS provider with the region `us-west-2`.
2. Creates an S3 bucket named `my-example-bucket-12345` with private ACL.
3. Attaches a CORS configuration to the S3 bucket with two rules:
   - The first rule allows `PUT` and `POST` methods from the specified origin with a max age of 3000 seconds.
   - The second rule allows `GET` method from any origin.

