### Description

This Terraform program sets up an AWS Lightsail Distribution with a Lightsail Instance as its origin. The configuration includes creating a Lightsail Instance, ensuring it has a static IP attached, and then setting up a Lightsail Distribution that points to this instance as its origin.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-1"
}

data "aws_availability_zones" "available" {
  state = "available"

  filter {
    name   = "opt-in-status"
    values = ["opt-in-not-required"]
  }
}

resource "aws_lightsail_static_ip" "test" {
  name = "test-static-ip"
}

resource "aws_lightsail_instance" "lightsail_instance_origin" {
  name              = "lightsail-origin-instance"
  availability_zone = data.aws_availability_zones.available.names[0]
  blueprint_id      = "amazon_linux_2"
  bundle_id         = "micro_1_0"
}

resource "aws_lightsail_static_ip_attachment" "test" {
  static_ip_name = aws_lightsail_static_ip.test.name
  instance_name  = aws_lightsail_instance.lightsail_instance_origin.name
}

resource "aws_lightsail_distribution" "lightsail_distribution" {
  name       = "lightsail-distribution"
  depends_on = [aws_lightsail_static_ip_attachment.test]
  bundle_id  = "small_1_0"

  origin {
    name        = aws_lightsail_instance.lightsail_instance_origin.name
    region_name = data.aws_availability_zones.available.names[0]
  }

  default_cache_behavior {
    behavior = "cache"
  }
}
```

### Explanation

1. **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured to use the `us-east-1` region.
2. **Availability Zones Data Source**: This data source fetches available availability zones in the specified region.
3. **Static IP Resource**: A static IP is created for the Lightsail Instance.
4. **Lightsail Instance Resource**: A Lightsail Instance is created with a specified availability zone, blueprint ID, and bundle ID.
5. **Static IP Attachment Resource**: The static IP is attached to the Lightsail Instance.
6. **Lightsail Distribution Resource**: A Lightsail Distribution is created with the instance as its origin. The distribution depends on the static IP attachment to ensure the instance has a static IP before the distribution is set up. The default cache behavior is set to "cache".

