### Description
This Terraform configuration creates an Application Load Balancer (ALB) with a listener that has a fixed-response action. The fixed-response action returns a plain text message with a 200 status code.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_lb" "front_end" {
  name               = "front-end-alb"
  internal           = false
  load_balancer_type = "application"
  subnets            = ["subnet-0123456789abcdef0", "subnet-0fedcba9876543210"]
  security_groups    = ["sg-0123456789abcdef0"]

  tags = {
    Name = "FrontEndALB"
  }
}

resource "aws_lb_listener" "front_end" {
  load_balancer_arn = aws_lb.front_end.arn
  port              = "80"
  protocol          = "HTTP"

  default_action {
    type = "fixed-response"

    fixed_response {
      content_type = "text/plain"
      message_body = "Fixed response content"
      status_code  = "200"
    }
  }
}
```

### Explanation
1. **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured to use the `us-west-2` region.
2. **Load Balancer (ALB)**: An Application Load Balancer is created with the name `front-end-alb`. It is set to be internet-facing (`internal = false`) and uses two subnets and a security group.
3. **Listener**: A listener is attached to the ALB on port 80 with the HTTP protocol. The listener has a default action of type `fixed-response`, which returns a plain text message with a 200 status code.

This configuration ensures that the Load Balancer and Listener are correctly set up with the specified fixed-response action.

